Basic Java assignment

1. How Java differs from other programming language like C?
Java and C are different in many ways, C is a Procedural language Focuses on functions and step by step instructions, While java is object oriented like class and object based.
Java runs on JVM, is platform independent, has automatic memory management, and is more secure compared to C.
C runs directly on the machine and needs manual memory handling

2.How to check the version of java in command prompt?
Open command prompt, type: java -version and press enter.then its shows the installed version

3.If i write a java program in Linux OS, is it possible to run in Windows OS? possible means why it is possible?
Yes, it is possible to run a Java program on windows because Java programs are compiled into bytecode, which runs inside the JVM, JVM is available for different operating systems like Linux and Windows, 
the same Java program can run on any system. this feature is called Write Once, Runs Anywhere

4.Why we are using Selenium with Java instead of other combination like Selenium + Ruby or Selenium+ Python?
Selenium can work with python and ruby , but java preferred because it is stable, widely used and has strong oop support.
Most companies already use Java,so selenium + Java is industry standard



